ass_mp: compact high-overdraw atlases

A sign made of many large, overlapping libass masks can need an atlas far
bigger than the frame it covers. The Ex2 sample's hold sign is 131 blurred
drawings, 153 Mpx of masks on a 4K canvas: the atlas exceeds what
mp_image_alloc accepts, packing fails and the sign is never shown. When a
VO takes both formats, flatten such a list into BGRA before packing: only
when the masks occupy more than four times the composited RGBA area in
bytes, so ordinary dialogue and animation stay on the cheap mask path.
Transparent pixels are skipped and opaque ones copied directly during the
composition. Tracks that need per-mask VSFilter color correction keep their
masks.

